## Medical disclaimer

This repository is an evidence review and educational resource. It is **not
medical advice**, and it does not create a clinician-patient relationship.

- Vitamin D and vitamin K are nutrients with real physiological effects and real
  interactions. Doses that are appropriate for one person may be unsafe for
  another.
- Do not start, stop, or change a supplement, or change the dose of a prescription
  medicine, on the basis of this document alone.
- People who are pregnant or breastfeeding, who have kidney disease, liver
  disease, hypercalcemia, granulomatous disease, cancer, hyperparathyroidism,
  malabsorption, a bleeding disorder, or who take anticoagulants or other
  interacting medications should consult a qualified clinician.
- If you suspect vitamin D toxicity or an adverse reaction, seek medical care.
